  <model metaid="meta_enalapril_kidney" id="enalapril_kidney" name="Model for renal enalapril and enalaprilat excretion." substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Model for the renal excretion of enalapril and enalaprilat.</p>
        <p>Enalapril and enalaprilat are excreted unchanged in the urine (filtration
and tubular secretion), no other metabolites are found. After 10 mg of
enalapril maleate about 25 % of the dose are recovered as enalapril and
35 % as enalaprilat {Ishizaki1988, Ohnishi1989}, 45 % after 20 mg
(3.41 mg enalapril, 3.78 mg enalaprilat) {Burckhardt2015}.</p>
        <p>The renal clearances are given relative to the filtration of the unbound
fraction, <code>GFR * fu</code>, and scale with the renal function: <code>GFR = f_renal_function * GFR_base</code>, the healthy GFR <code>GFR_base</code> (101 ml/min at
75 kg) is replaced by the body model.</p>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
