    <listOfParameters>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="f_renal_function" name="renal function" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <blockquote>
              <p>1.0: increased kidney function
1.0: normal kidney function (healthy control)
&lt;1.0: decreased kidney function</p>
            </blockquote>
            <p>Renal function relative to the healthy glomerular filtration rate
GFR_base, which is 101 ml/min at 75 kg; a measured creatinine
clearance of X ml/min is the renal function X/101.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="GFR_base" name="glomerular filtration rate (healthy)" value="101" units="ml_per_min" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="fu_ena" name="fraction unbound in plasma enalapril" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>Replaced by the body model.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="fu_eat" name="fraction unbound in plasma enalaprilat" value="0.62" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>Replaced by the body model.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="ENAEX_f" name="renal clearance of unbound enalapril relative to the GFR" value="2.87792398538051" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>The renal clearance of enalapril is ENAEX_f times the filtration
of its unbound fraction, fu_ena * GFR: 1 is filtration alone, above
1 a net secretion, below 1 a net reabsorption.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
